PolicyManagerCancelByProofsTest
├── When no attempt was ever recorded
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt, never PolicyManager_NoSetup, and call no method.
├── When a setup exists but no attempt was ever opened
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt and call no method.
├── When the attempt was already cancelled
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt and leave the record untouched.
├── When the attempt was consumed
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt.
├── When the attempt id is not the live one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongAttemptId carrying both ids and call no method.
├── When the attempt id is the next one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongAttemptId naming the live id.
├── When the request names a nonce other than the stored one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongSetupNonce carrying both nonces and call no method.
├── When the window has passed
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_RequestExpired carrying both times and call no method.
├── When the window ends in this block
│   └── It should cancel the attempt.
├── When the attempt was judged under another nonce
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_StaleAttempt carrying both nonces and call no method.
├── When the setup is gone but a record still waits
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_SetupCommitmentMismatch against the zero commitment, never PolicyManager_NoSetup.
├── When no attempt waits and every other check fails
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt.
├── When the nonce the id and the window all fail
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongSetupNonce.
├── When the nonce and the window both fail
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongSetupNonce.
├── When the id and the window both fail
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongAttemptId.
├── When the window has passed and the body does not match
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_RequestExpired.
├── When the attempt is stale and the body does not match
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_StaleAttempt.
├── When the body does not hash to the commitment
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_SetupCommitmentMismatch carrying both commitments and call no method.
├── When the proofs sign the approval digest
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When the proofs were signed for another attempt
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When each method is asked
│   └── It should hand each method the cancellation digest of its place, its config and its proof once, by a static call.
├── When a place repeats the previous one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_PlacesNotStrictlyIncreasing.
├── When a place is past the end of the rule
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_PlaceOutOfRange.
├── When the proof names another method of the rule
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_CredentialMismatch and never ask that method about the place.
├── When a proof names a method the rule never names
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_CredentialMismatch and never call that method.
├── When the proof carries another config
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_CredentialMismatch and never call the method.
├── When a method reports itself stopped
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodStopped before its verify is called.
├── When the body ignores stops
│   └── It should cancel without reading any pause.
├── When the body ignores stops but the record does not
│   └── It should cancel without reading any pause.
├── When the record ignores stops but the body does not
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodStopped.
├── When the pause read reverts
│   └── It should cancel the attempt.
├── When the method reverts
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When the method returns nothing
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When the method returns more than a word
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When the method returns another word
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When the method writes state while verifying
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected and leave the method's storage untouched.
├── When the method returns a huge answer
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected on a gas budget that copying the answer would exhaust.
├── When the set is too weak to open
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_RuleUnsatisfied naming the clause.
├── When the request carries no proofs
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_RuleUnsatisfied and call no method.
├── When a satisfying set cancels
│   ├── It should set the attempt to Cancelled and keep the rest of its record.
│   ├── It should emit AttemptCancelled alone.
│   └── It should leave the setup and the attempt counter unchanged.
├── When the same cancellation is sent twice
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt.
└── When an attempt opens after the cancel
    └── It should open the next id.
